        <div class="product-summary">
          <h1>ST-S200 Mini Ionizing Air Blower</h1>
          <p class="product-short-desc">
            The smallest unit in the range — 128 × 53.5 × 180 mm and 400 g, small enough to
            build into a machine rather than stand beside one. Synchronous positive and
            negative emitters at ±5000 V with tungsten-alloy tips clear a 450 × 450 mm area
            in under 1.5 s, at under 38.9 dB and 0.05 ppm ozone. CE marked, one-year warranty.
          </p>

          <div class="product-actions">
            <button class="quote-btn" type="button">Get a Quote</button>
            <a href="https://wa.me/61436605126" target="_blank" class="whatsapp-btn">WhatsApp</a>
          </div>

          <dl class="key-specs">
            <div><dt>Coverage area</dt><dd><strong>450 × 450 mm</strong></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Decay time</dt><dd><strong>≤1.5 s</strong> at 150 mm from the outlet</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Airflow / noise</dt><dd><strong>≤48.2 CFM</strong> · ≤38.9 dB at 1 m</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Size / weight</dt><dd><strong>128 × 53.5 × 180 mm</strong> · 400 g</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Certification</dt><dd><strong>CE</strong> · one-year warranty</dd></div>
          </dl>
          <p class="key-specs-note">Small enough to build into a machine rather than stand beside one. Ozone stays at or below 0.05 ppm.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="detail-block pd-section">
        <h2>What the ST-S200 Fixes</h2>
        <p class="pd-lede">If any of these is happening on your line, the cause is usually a surface charge nobody is measuring.</p>
        <div class="pd-fix">
          <div class="pd-fix-item">
            <h3>Charge on parts that are not moving</h3>
            <p>A bar neutralizes material passing in front of it. When the charge is on a stationary part, a stack, or an operator&#39;s hands, nothing passes the bar.</p>
            <span class="sol">Ionized air carried to the area</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pd-fix-item">
            <h3>No room for a bench blower</h3>
            <p>Inside a machine enclosure, on a frame, or under a shelf there is often no space for a full-size unit.</p>
            <span class="sol">400 g, 180 mm tall, U-bracket included</span>
          </div>
          <div class="pd-fix-item">
            <h3>The blower is loud enough that operators switch it off</h3>
            <p>A unit that gets turned off protects nothing. Noise is a real reliability factor at a manned station.</p>
            <span class="sol">≤38.9 dB measured 1 m away</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="detail-block pd-section">
        <h2>How It Works</h2>
        <p class="pd-lede">Synchronous positive and negative emitter electrodes at ±5000 V produce a corona discharge at tungsten-alloy tips; an axial fan carries the ions to the surface.</p>
        <p>It is the smallest device Shidike makes. At 128 × 53.5 × 180 mm and 400 g it is designed to be mounted inside equipment as much as placed on a bench — the case is flame-retardant plastic and it ships with a stainless U-bracket and a pair of plastic thumb screws.</p>
        <p>The discharge structure is a decoupled barrel type, so there is no direct electrical contact at the emitter. Fan speed is adjustable across three settings, which is the practical control you have over the trade between decay time, airflow and noise.</p>
        <p>Where a bar neutralizes a line of material passing in front of it, the ST-S200 neutralizes an area: 450 × 450 mm, cleared in under 1.5 seconds measured 150 mm in front of the outlet.</p>
        <ul class="feature-list">
          <li>Compact body, straightforward to mount — including inside equipment where a bench unit will not fit</li>
          <li>Low power draw: 12 W fan plus 5 W ion generator</li>
          <li>Three-speed fan — high, medium, low</li>
          <li>Front and rear grilles are removable for cleaning and maintenance</li>
          <li>Tungsten-alloy emitters in a decoupled discharge barrel — no direct electrical contact to erode</li>
          <li>Supplied with a dedicated adapter: AC 100–240 V in, DC 24 V 1500 mA out</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

